{%- doc -%}
  The diamond shape the page the shopper is on is about, or nothing.

  The mega menu's Shop by Shape column opens a collection per cut - shape-round and
  friends under Jewellery, <cut>-engagement-rings under Engagement, <cut>-diamonds under
  Diamonds ('menu-static-items') - so a shopper who clicked Radiant has already said
  which cut they want. Every card on that page should answer in that cut: the photo,
  the icon underlined in the shape row, and the variant the card links to.
  'card-default-variant' is what turns this into that variant.

  Three sources, in priority order:

  - A Search & Discovery Shape filter comes from the filters Shopify reports as applied,
    the same way 'card-default-metal' reads the metal the grid is filtered to.
  - A native collection tag filter comes from 'current_tags'.
  - The collection handle. Read off the handle rather than kept in a list here, so a new
    shape collection needs nothing adding. Matching is on whole hyphen segments, which
    is what keeps "pearl-..." from reading as Pear.

  Outputs one lowercase shape key ("radiant"), or nothing on any page that is not about
  one cut. Only the ten cuts the theme draws an icon for are recognised - the same ten
  'menu-link-icon' and 'blocks/_card-product-shapes.liquid' carry - because a cut with
  no icon has nothing for a card to underline.

  Usage:
  {%- capture page_shape -%}{%- render 'shape-context' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign shape_keys = 'round,oval,cushion,emerald,princess,radiant,asscher,heart,marquise,pear' | split: ','
  assign page_shape = ''

  assign applied_filters = collection.filters
  if applied_filters == blank
    assign applied_filters = search.filters
  endif

  for applied_filter in applied_filters
    assign filter_label = applied_filter.label | downcase
    assign filter_names_shape = false
    if filter_label contains 'shape' or filter_label contains 'cut'
      assign filter_names_shape = true
    endif

    for applied_value in applied_filter.active_values
      assign filter_text = applied_value.value | downcase
      unless filter_names_shape or filter_text contains 'shape:'
        continue
      endunless
      for shape in shape_keys
        if filter_text contains shape
          assign page_shape = shape
          break
        endif
      endfor
      if page_shape != blank
        break
      endif
    endfor

    if page_shape != blank
      break
    endif
  endfor

  # Native collection tag filters use `/collections/<handle>/<tag-handle>` rather than a
  # `filter.p.tag` query parameter. The Shape tiles use that route so they still filter when
  # Shopify's Search & Discovery Tags filter is not enabled. Read the current tag here too,
  # so product cards open on the cut the shopper selected.
  if page_shape == blank
    for current_tag in current_tags
      assign filter_text = current_tag | downcase
      unless filter_text contains 'shape:'
        continue
      endunless
      for shape in shape_keys
        assign shape_tag = 'shape:' | append: shape
        if filter_text == shape_tag
          assign page_shape = shape
          break
        endif
      endfor
      if page_shape != blank
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  if page_shape == blank and collection != blank and collection.handle != blank
    assign handle_segments = collection.handle | split: '-'
    for segment in handle_segments
      if shape_keys contains segment
        assign page_shape = segment
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
{{- page_shape -}}
